  "result": "Perfect! All 219 tests pass. The customer statements feature is complete:\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **src/statements.js** \u2014 New module with two functions:\n   - `balanceDue(invoice)` \u2014 Calculates amount still owed on an invoice (total - payments)\n   - `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` \u2014 Generates customer statement\n     - Normalizes customer ID\n     - Filters invoices by:\n       - Customer match\n       - Status: 'issued' or 'partially_paid' only\n       - issueDate on or before asOf\n     - For each invoice returns: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n     - Sorts by issueDate ascending\n     - Returns `{ customerId, invoices, totalDue }`\n     - Error: `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` if customer doesn't exist\n\n2. **Test coverage** \u2014 19 comprehensive tests verifying:\n   - Unknown customer rejection\n   - Empty statements\n   - Single and multiple invoice handling\n   - All invoice fields included correctly\n   - Partial payment calculations\n   - Draft invoice exclusion\n   - Date filtering (asOf dates)\n   - Sorting by issueDate\n   - Total due summation\n   - Multi-customer invoice filtering\n   - Partially paid status handling\n   - Paid invoice exclusion\n   - Customer ID normalization (case and spaces)\n   - Voucher interaction\n   - Complex scenarios with mixed payment statuses\n\n**Total: 219 tests passing** (200 + 19 new)",
